<title>USA: TABLE - PSt Vans Q2 shr profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>TABLE - PSt Vans Q2 shr profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>SALT LAKE CITY 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended	     Six months ended</p>
<p>		  June 30,    June 30,	 June 30,    June 30,</p>
<p>		   1997	  1996	     1997	  1996</p>
<p>Revenues   $35,313,910   $36,428,193  $69,836,519  $74,664,217</p>
<p>Operating Income (loss)</p>
<p>		 $1,249,223    (65,828)	236,883	 118,863</p>
<p>Net Income (Loss)</p>
<p>		 $183,730  ($1,311,297)  ($1,925,346) ($2,448,453)</p>
<p>Net Income (Loss) Per Common Share</p>
<p>		 $0.04	  ($0.31)	 ($0.46)	  ($0.58)</p>
<p>Weighted Average Common Shares Outstanding</p>
<p>		 4,227,215    4,209,409    4,226,880     4,209,409</p>
<p>NOTE: -- Norton attributed the nearly $2 million bottom-line improvement versus first quarter results primarily to continuing progress in a number of operational areas, including equipment utilization, overhead costs and insurance claims expense.</p>
<p>-- Company says it reduced administrative staff levels by 11 percent in Q2 as part of move to contain costs.</p>
<p>-- Company says cash position is $2.1 million.</p>
